The diagnostic points at the nested function that crosses the clause’s boundary. Even calling later immediately does not make this capture valid. Keep the resume 2 directly in the operation clause. Ordinary helper functions can compute the integer answer, but cannot capture this right to resume. The effect rules define these consumption and scope restrictions.

Ask the handler whether to continue
02-stop-at-zero.ash makes reaching zero an operation request instead:
type Scores = End
    | Item(Int, Scores)
type Outcome = Finished(Int)
    | Stopped(Int)

effect Stop {
    at_zero : Int -&gt; Unit
}

sum_scores : (Scores, Int) -&gt; Int ! {Stop}
sum_scores (End, total) = total
sum_scores (Item(value, rest), total) = {
    let ignored = match value == 0 {
        true =&gt; perform Stop.at_zero total
        false =&gt; ()
    }
    sum_scores (rest, total + value)
}

main : Unit -&gt; Outcome
main () = {
    let values = Item(20, Item(0, Item(99, End)))
    handle (Finished (sum_scores (values, 0))) with Stop {
        at_zero partial =&gt; {
            let ignored = discard
            Stopped partial
        }
    }
}
The operation carries the partial total and expects a Unit answer. If it receives that answer, the calculation can continue to its recursive call. The surrounding handler instead executes discard, consuming the continuation without running the waiting remainder. The clause then returns Stopped partial. discard itself returns Unit, which the ignored binding sets aside.
At the zero request, identify the accumulated prefix and all the waiting work. Follow the call back to main as well: what must happen before Finished can be constructed? Predict the clause’s outcome after discard:
$ ash 02-stop-at-zero.ash
Stopped(20) : Outcome
The request carries 20. Discard abandons the recursive call that would visit 99 and the pending outer construction of Finished. The clause instead constructs Stopped(20), producing the same outcome as the pure version. The difference is where the stopping choice lives. The pure function chooses in its match. The effectful function requests a decision; its handler chooses how to consume the waiting continuation.

Choose to continue instead
In 03-continue-at-zero.ash, the calculation and input are unchanged. The clause supplies the operation’s Unit answer through resume ():
