Both items take the recursive branch, so no request occurs. The body finishes with Finished(42); the discarding clause never runs. The static Stop row still describes what sum_scores may require for other inputs. The handler supplies that contract even when one execution does not request it. The evaluation rules distinguish a handler body’s normal return from a selected clause’s consumption of waiting work.
The effect rules also check whether abandoned work can be closed safely. These examples own no resources or cleanup actions. Do not conclude that every discard is pure or that it can skip any enclosing obligation. We will return to those questions after introducing scoped state and cleanup.

