6 | stop_while_closing ignored = perform Stop.now ()
  |                              ^ This request or call can capture the continuation.
  --&gt; /path/to/ash-doc/content/effects/running-cleanup/src/06-running-action.ash:9:18
9 | main () = handle (cleanup stop_while_closing {
  |                  ^ This cleanup action must complete.
10 |     42
   | ^ This cleanup action must complete.
11 | }) with Stop {
   | ^ This cleanup action must complete.
reason: effect.discard-unsafe
Discard would skip the rest of the action and its unfinished close operation. The labels identify that required completion and the request that captures it. Use resume () in the stop clause to let the action finish. Resumption continues that invocation; it does not start the cleanup action again.
These rules govern normal completion and checked abandonment. They do not promise source cleanup after internal termination or exhaustion, and they do not prove that a diverging action eventually returns.

effect Adjust {
    publish : Int -&gt; Int
}

increment : Int -&gt; Int
increment value = value + 1

double : Int -&gt; Int
double value = value * 2

main : Unit -&gt; Int
main () = hook Adjust {
    register Adjust increment {
        register Adjust double {
            perform Adjust.publish 3
        }
