The first lookup follows 3 → 2 → 1 → 0. Compression then writes 0 into entries 1, 2, and 3, so the next lookup follows only 3 → 0. It still writes entry 3 on return, even though that parent is already 0. Without compression, both lookups follow the original four-entry chain.
