The primary label covers the buffer body that returns next. The related label begins at the buffer acquisition owning that access. Inside the function, Buffer.read still needs buffer; capturing the enclosing position cell does not preserve the buffer’s lifetime. Even leaving escaped unused cannot make that returned dependency valid. The secondary reason is type.resource-escape.
The dependency rules follow retained access through closures and outcome wrappers. A result type without an explicit handle field is not enough to erase that dependency. Keep the reads and cursor updates inside their live owners and return the copied integers in ordinary message data instead. 06-decode-in-scope.ash uses run_frame, whose decoding happens before those scopes close:
import @ffi.native_buffer as Buffer
import frames as Frames
import codec as Codec

main : Unit -&gt; Buffer.Outcome&lt;Buffer.Outcome&lt;Frames.DecodeResult&gt;&gt;
main () = Codec.run_frame (
    3, Frames.Byte(2, Frames.Byte(0, Frames.Byte(255, Frames.End)))
)
Build and run the repaired entry:
Success(Success(Decoded(Pair(0, 255))))
The returned Pair(0,255) retains only ordinary integer fields. The outer and inner success wrappers remain visible after access ends. The complete human message records this edition’s tool presentation; its wording and printed layout are not a language contract.
